by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-13T10:40:26Z

Rebased on 7.4 and reworked the check.

Reverted the requoting of the `LogicException` messages: those are fabbot false positives, and the messages are unrelated to this fix.

Swapped `filter_var()` for an `is_numeric()` gate that throws and then leaves the value alone, so PHP keeps coercing it exactly as it does today. `is_numeric()` is not an approximation here, it is precisely the set that separates working input from a `TypeError`:

| input | today | `is_numeric` | `FILTER_VALIDATE_INT` |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `07`, `007` | 7 | yes | reject |
| `1e3` | 1000 | yes | reject |
| `12.0` | 12 | yes | reject |
| `0x1A`, `1_000`, `12abc`, `abc`, ``, `3,14` | TypeError | no | reject |

Every value that throws a `TypeError` today for a non-numeric reason is rejected, and nothing that works today stops working, which is what a patch release needs. `FILTER_VALIDATE_INT` would have refused zero-padded integers, and `--month=07` or a zero-padded id is ordinary on a command line. `FILTER_FLAG_ALLOW_OCTAL` is not a way out, since it would read `010` as 8.

@GromNaN this answers the question you raised about `007`: with this shape it stays valid.

Tests now use `abc` for the rejected case, since `1.5` for an `int` is accepted today (it truncates with PHP’s own precision deprecation, which the gate leaves in place), plus a case pinning that `007` and `1e3` still convert. Both tests fail on 7.4 with the `TypeError` this PR removes.

Two things left out on purpose, both pre-existing and neither the reported bug: an out-of-range value such as `9223372036854775808` still raises a `TypeError`, and `#[Argument, Ask]` on a `MapInput` property writes the answer straight to the typed property without passing through `resolveValue()`, so a bad interactive answer still raises one too.
